{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":887498,"title":"The American West in the World of Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-10T14:31:33-07:00","id":887498,"title":"The American West in the World of Darkness?","content":"This is probably a silly question but were there any books or settings for WoD that revolved around the American West? I think I remember some material for Werewolf, but did anything come out for Vampire, or Hunter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:47:51-07:00","id":887512,"title":"","content":"THe World of Darkness, formerly the Old World of Darkness, had Werewolf: THe Wild West.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness, formerly the New World of Darkness, <i>could</i> have had the Wild West as a Geist setting in Dark Eras, but <i>some mass of people</i> didn't think that would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am still bitter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:58:59-07:00","id":887522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=887512#post887512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe World of Darkness, formerly the Old World of Darkness, had Werewolf: THe Wild West.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness, formerly the New World of Darkness, <i>could</i> have had the Wild West as a Geist setting in Dark Eras, but <i>some mass of people</i> didn't think that would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am still bitter.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a member of Geist's small but loyal fanbase, I am also somewhat salty.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if I died, GtSE would be one of my anchors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:12:20-07:00","id":887537,"title":"","content":"Okay, So I just looked up Dark Eras. Some really great material there. But you're right, nothing specific to the American West. Thank you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> for the heads up. P.S. Sorry to here that Geist didn't work out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:16:21-07:00","id":887542,"title":"","content":"Call me Arc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:59:05-07:00","id":887577,"title":"","content":"That was a MAJOR disappointment for me as well. The American West is a time period with an amazing amount of story potential, and even overlaps with Victorian England for a bit more globetrotting.<br /> For the Western Era games I have run in CofD, the only real adjustments are a few skill adjustments ( Computers for Enigmas or Travel and Drive for Ride) and maybe a few equipment alterations ( reduce range, accuracy, or damage for most firearms and the equipment bonus for many items to reflect the less sophisticated technology).<br /> <br /> Beyond that, its just a matter of getting in enough research to get the proper feel for the era. I recommend Werewolf:the Wild West, Deadlands, and Gurps: The Old West for some good information that should get you started. Ken Burns - The West is a good documentary, and watching any number of westerns if you want more cinematic than historical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:04:28-07:00","id":887640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=887512#post887512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe World of Darkness, formerly the Old World of Darkness, had Werewolf: THe Wild West.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness, formerly the New World of Darkness, <i>could</i> have had the Wild West as a Geist setting in Dark Eras, but <i>some mass of people</i> didn't think that would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am still bitter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> too many good options. We missed Pirates too .... Dark Eras 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:23:11-07:00","id":887665,"title":"","content":"Not that I agree on pirates, but why go for good when we could've had the best?<br /> <br /> Mind you, I say this basically having praised to heavens every choice I thought was gonna be lame, so I don't actually have a leg to stand on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:17:26-07:00","id":887710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>R.Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness#post887498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a silly question but were there any books or settings for WoD that revolved around the American West? I think I remember some material for Werewolf, but did anything come out for Vampire, or Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient Mysteries for Vampire has a chapter (and corresponding material in its sister book, Ancient Bloodlines) on an ill-fortuned westward settlement party that departed Kansas for Oregon in the 1800s, and the troubles they encountered along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:52:56-07:00","id":887813,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> Thanks for the tips. Yeah, I've long thought setting a game in the West at the tail end of the 1800s would be great fun especially for something like vampire. The travel options would be incredibly limited for the undead. It would make for some really interesting concepts. Traveling circus/theatre troupe maybe? Maybe the mayor of a local settlement has made a deal with a vampire to bring in settlers...I don't know. Or maybe a game that uses the Donner party as a jumping off point. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> I'll look into that one, sounds really interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:06:06-07:00","id":888210,"title":"","content":"We are getting Reconstruction Era Beast as an additional Dark Era from its Kickstarter, don't remember the exact location though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:54:54-07:00","id":888531,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for specifically Chronicles stuff, I did stat up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/81977-the-man-with-no-name\">the Man With No Name</a> here.<br /> <br /> Man, a Geist Western setting would be pretty awesome. Combine it with, what, Werewolf? Or maybe go really unorthodox and go with Vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:36:44-07:00","id":888690,"title":"","content":"Wandering frontier hero would work well for a Promethean; they can take any damn thing other non-supernaturals can dish out, then ride into the sunset before Disquiet sets in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T23:47:45-07:00","id":888899,"title":"","content":"The town of Tombstone was definitely founded by a Mummy cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:17:14-07:00","id":889089,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a> Why would Vampire be considered unorthodox for a western setting? I'm not being flippant, I have my own ideas, but I would love to hear your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:21:39-07:00","id":889130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>R.Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=889089#post889089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a> Why would Vampire be considered unorthodox for a western setting? I'm not being flippant, I have my own ideas, but I would love to hear your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Claire (obviously), but if I had to guess, I'd say it would be very restricted due to the wide open expanses, increasing risk of sun exposure and decreasing food supply. A low Blood Potency Gangrel might swing it by operating at night, but other types would be greatly disadvantaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:30:56-07:00","id":889258,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> Got it. However, those are the same reason's I find it so interesting as a Vampire setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:52:06-07:00","id":889274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=889130#post889130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Claire (obviously), but if I had to guess, I'd say it would be very restricted due to the wide open expanses, increasing risk of sun exposure and decreasing food supply. A low Blood Potency Gangrel might swing it by operating at night, but other types would be greatly disadvantaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree, but I think having a situation where you're forced to solve those problems could be very interesting. Perhaps you take the role of a crusading lawman specifically to keep up Humanity and minimize sun risk. Maybe you take control of a small town and operate from inside dark saloons, operating solely through proxies. Maybe you manipulate things to bring modern transportation to the west faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:49:19-07:00","id":889300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=889274#post889274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you manipulate things to bring modern transportation to the west faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just thinking you could set up a conflict between the &quot;moneyed&quot; Rail Baron Vampires, and the independent frontier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:17:02-07:00","id":889390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>R.Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=889089#post889089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a> Why would Vampire be considered unorthodox for a western setting? I'm not being flippant, I have my own ideas, but I would love to hear your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unorthodox, though not inappropriate. But so much of the Western atmosphere is dusty, sun-baked vistas and parched towns as cracked and dried as a cowboy's lips. Vampires only coming out at night would be an interesting contrast with the burning daytime scenes. It could be fun. Duels at High Midnight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:45:18-07:00","id":890327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a> Gotcha. You're right, the popular ideas of &quot;westerns&quot; don't seem to suit the Material in Vampire at first glance, there are hidden ideas to mine from the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T19:18:28-07:00","id":890338,"title":"","content":"I'm all for going with unorthodox things. In fact, it's one of my favorite things to do in gaming. It's certainly not a bad word. And some of the tropes work well. In fact, you could use the contrast between cool desert nights and burning days would make for some evocative themes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T03:21:13-07:00","id":890524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=888210#post888210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are getting Reconstruction Era Beast as an additional Dark Era from its Kickstarter, don't remember the exact location though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it's Reconstruction... so it's the southern states (the former Confederacy). It might be more specific than that (looking specifically at a given state or city), but it won't be the western territories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-14-2016, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T03:24:19-07:00","id":890526,"title":"","content":"I stand by my view that the #1 fit for a Wild West Era would be Demon. People escaping into the &quot;wilderness&quot; to build new lives for themselves while the iron tendrils of the industrializing East chase behind them via the rise of the railroad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T03:26:50-07:00","id":890528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=887512#post887512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe World of Darkness, formerly the Old World of Darkness, had Werewolf: THe Wild West.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness, formerly the New World of Darkness, <i>could</i> have had the Wild West as a Geist setting in Dark Eras, but <i>some mass of people</i> didn't think that would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am still bitter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *goes back to check*<br /> <br /> Well it lost to what ended up becoming the Wolf &amp; the Raven (Werewolf &amp; Geist Vikings), for whatever that is worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:33:33-07:00","id":890617,"title":"","content":"Lots of tiny communities separated by hundreds of miles of lonely train whistles. Lots of ignorant settlers who can be convinced that violence is the work of wolves and savages. Lots of room for charismatic fire-and-brimstone preachers, big toothy grins selling big shiny bottles of cure-all, reclusive drunken Civil War sawbones whose patients <i>don't </i>complain of crippling agony afterwards, weird incestuous cults in Utah, sheep ranchers grinning and wiping their rivals' livelihood off their lips, saloons where every ounce of whiskey passes under same pair of slim, pale hands after dark, swarms of grim, silent Natives in the night who have reluctantly accepted one Curse or another to effectively return fire...<br /> <br /> A lot of the mortal infrastructure that supports vampires isn't there, but there's... niches, if you know where to look, and you're willing to risk tapdancing on quicksand night to night.<br /> <br /> Just like the settlers, come to think.<br /> <br /> Also it makes a kickass start to a historic-to-modern game; trying to hit up the Conclave for favors and being told &quot;dude, no. That dandy pissant in Tulsa that swore vengeance after you gunned down his Touchstone in the street has been Prince for like twenty years. Maybe see if anyone at the Reservation remembers your name instead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 05-16-2016, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:39:35-07:00","id":890644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=890528#post890528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *goes back to check*<br /> <br /> Well it lost to what ended up becoming the Wolf &amp; the Raven (Werewolf &amp; Geist Vikings), for whatever that is worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in the end, I still really liked The Wolf and The Raven, in fact I was surprised by how much I liked it-which can be said of most settings from the voting process I thought were going to be stupid.<br /> <br /> BUT WE COULD HAVE HAD SIN-EATERS BANDITS!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:23:15-07:00","id":890706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=890528#post890528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *goes back to check*<br /> <br /> Well it lost to what ended up becoming the Wolf &amp; the Raven (Werewolf &amp; Geist Vikings), for whatever that is worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>and that explains my vote. Wasn't a matter of thinking cowboys wouldn't be awesome, just that vikings sounded more awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:26:47-07:00","id":890708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=890644#post890644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the end, I still really liked The Wolf and The Raven, in fact I was surprised by how much I liked it-which can be said of most settings from the voting process I thought were going to be stupid.<br /> <br /> BUT WE COULD HAVE HAD SIN-EATERS BANDITS!</div> </div> </div> </div>hey maybe you could write the chapter for us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm pretty sure we'd all drool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:27:46-07:00","id":890710,"title":"","content":"Why not narrow down a region and time period and collectively work on ideas from there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-14-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:46:50-07:00","id":890722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=890708#post890708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey maybe you could write the chapter for us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm pretty sure we'd all drool</div> </div> </div> </div>Flatterring. It'd fun, and I'd be up for it, but I'm pretty sure I'd only get hired if they decided to focus on the Deseret Territory, and we have Dogs in the Vineyard for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:51:46-07:00","id":890769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=888531#post888531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking for specifically Chronicles stuff, I did stat up <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/81977-the-man-with-no-name\">the Man With No Name</a> here.<br /> <br /> Man, a Geist Western setting would be pretty awesome. Combine it with, what, Werewolf? Or maybe go really unorthodox and go with Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rE-chhwi0bw\" target=\"_blank\">I'll pass on Old West Vampires</a>.<br /> <br /> OK, more seriously - while I'd have no problem with Vampire gunslingers (Celerity Devotion's on me, boys!), I'd like to see Wild West Changeling.<br /> <br /> Or Hunter. Wild West Hunter would be great - imagine Hunter in an Era where the proper response to &quot;no good supernatural rascals&quot; is &quot;I'll warm up the posse&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:13:47-07:00","id":890833,"title":"","content":"I'd go Promethean or Mummy for a second on Sin-Eater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:55:53-07:00","id":891446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=890833#post890833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go Promethean or Mummy for a second on Sin-Eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... But... Demons seeking to find their Hells in the West, being chased by the iron tendrils of the God Machine via encroaching railroads and telegraph lines, etc etc.<br /> <br /> I'll trade you Wild West for Demons in return for Great War for Geist* (when the Horsemen themselves quite possibly strode the Earth)!<br /> <br /> *Werewolves as their second string","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/for