onouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T18:07:27-07:00","id":891482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=891479#post891479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Demons have more of a place Back East anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the point of the given narrative would be trying to escape the infrastructure of the Machine, to build their Hell on the frontier, just like other settlers running away from their pasts or trying to find their fortune, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:01:29-07:00","id":891537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=891482#post891482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the point of the given narrative would be trying to escape the infrastructure of the Machine, to build their Hell on the frontier, just like other settlers running away from their pasts or trying to find their fortune, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>now I'm imagining a train that is infrastructure, and demon's executing a train &quot;robbery&quot; on horseback...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:07:00-07:00","id":891560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=891537#post891537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now I'm imagining a <b>train that is infrastructure</b>, and demon's executing a train &quot;robbery&quot; on horseback...</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh-oh.<br /> <br /> Another opportunity to shoehorn in a personally <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oi5-wG_wf-E\" target=\"_blank\">favorite</a> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AfterlifeExpress\" target=\"_blank\">trope </a>of mine.<br /> <br /> Who says ghosts can't be productive? <b> All Aboard.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> ...Also, I just realized that no techgnostic discussion involving trains would be complete without-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://darktower.wikia.com/wiki/Blaine_the_Mono\" target=\"_blank\">Blaine the Brain</a> Is a Major Pain. Choo-Choo. <br /> <i>Choo-Choo Choo-Choo.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:40:32-07:00","id":891724,"title":"","content":"I think I am drawn to this genre particularly with regard to CoD, because I was raised and still live in the West. There is more here that dust covered vistas, although those are usually what people think of. Denver itself was a hub of activity during the 1800s. Anyway, regardless of game, the western genre is an interesting thing to play around with. Hunter* is a natural fit, in my opinion, with plenty of opportunity to work in real historical figures like Buffalo Bill Cody (A possible inspiration for Stoker\u2019s Dracula, BTW) but I keep thinking about Vampire because the weaknesses offer opportunities for several interesting plot hooks.<br /> <br /> -A medicine cart travels the West with a list of settlements to visit, offering tiny free bottles of a new product to those in need. But only the first taste is free and if you want more of this magnificent miracle cure, you'll have to talk to the cart driver's boss, a mysterious benefactor only seen at night.<br /> <br /> -A group of vampires find themselves marooned in Colorado territory after running afoul of their city's Prince. Desperate they find themselves drawn to a mining camp to sustain themselves. Realizing that the local cathouse is run by an unscrupulous businessman, they decide to take over.<br /> <br /> -A city\u2019s prince send an emissaries to Leadville Colorado, to view a theatrical production mounted at the Tabor Opera House. The production claims to tell of \u201cSupernatural creatures hiding in our very midst\u201d. Is this stage play a breach of secrets? Or is it an elaborate trap?<br /> <br /> -The Transcontinental Railroad is now complete! The future is in the American west and we now have the iron bests to take us there. Not wishing to rest on your laurels, you board a train to San Francisco to establish yourself in the burgeoning cities growing in the American frontier. This particular railway line is known for luxury, offering the denizens of New York an escape to the romance of the west. There are plenty of young, rich and beautiful people from which to choose. However, the old Pinkerton agent seems a tad familiar. Have we run into him before?<br /> <br /> <i>*I actually have a Great War Hunter setting I\u2019ve been tinkering with for a while but that\u2019s neither hither nor thither.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>R. Walker<br /> Creator of Victorian Cut-out Theatre. Writer, punch up artist and promos.","edited":{"userid":10271,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","user":"R.Walker","date":". 05-16-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10271-r-walker","name":"R.Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:22:57-07:00","id":891749,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Vampire <i>can</i> be run, with circumventing the inherent limitations serving as excellent fodder for plot ideas.<ul><li>A local gang of bandits has recently added kidnapping to their list of crimes. Law enforcement reports them having freakish strength and uncanny talents at stealth. [A vampire has set themselves up as a bandit king, Ghouling the Bandits to make them more effective. Any final confrontation will of course take place in their abandoned mine hideout.]</li> <li>The famous (in infamous, depending on who you talk to) Jebediah Stone, was scheduled to be hanged for a series of murders ending with that of the local mine foreman. Except, it is called off after the murders continue even while Stone is locked up, and the mine foreman was even spotted walking around a few nights later. [A Kindred is preying on the local community and has even started Embracing some of their victims.]</li> </ul><br /> I'm actually trying to think of which game-lines <i>wouldn't</i> fit in the West. Mummy, maybe?<ul><li>Vampire: Fits, once their vulnerabilities are taken into account.</li> <li>Werewolf: Fits like a well worn glove.</li> <li>Mage: Occult mysteries found in places only lightly touched by humanity. Things better left forgotten uncovered in the lust for gold. What looks like ordinary mysteries taking a turn for the strange in isolated towns.</li> <li>Promethean: Fits in with the themes of wanderers and looking for a place to belong.</li> <li>Changeling: Interfaces with the &quot;narrative&quot; aspects, such as wandering heroes and tall tales.</li> <li>Hunter: Monsters go bump in the night regardless of the level of civilization. You and your posse standing alone as defenders of some frontier town captures the &quot;candle in the darkness&quot; feel of the Vigil.</li> <li>Geist: Ghost stories. Tales of revenge from beyond the grave. Crimes of the past brought to light. Second Chances.</li> <li>Mummy: ???</li> <li>Demon: Keeping hidden from the powers that be and carving out your own place. Plenty of weird places that could serve as discarded Infrastructure in the West.</li> <li>Beast: Fears aplenty plague those on the fringes. Also, even many of the &quot;heroes&quot; were people treated with a certain amount of fear mixed in with the respect.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-16-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:32:16-07:00","id":891756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=890524#post890524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well it's Reconstruction... so it's the southern states (the former Confederacy). It might be more specific than that (looking specifically at a given state or city), but it won't be the western territories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, its not quite the right location, but it is the right time period and a close location. It should provide some inspiration at least. I suppose I could have been more clear that I knew it wasn't really <b>The West</b> but I assumed that to be known from the Reconstruction part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T20:40:49-07:00","id":913193,"title":"","content":"I am currently running a Hunter game set in 1881 Colorado Springs. The characters are part of a fledgling Project Valkyrie that has sent cells out west as part of Operation Trailblazer, an attempt to discover how far and how deep the supernatural menace goes. <br /> <br /> Colorado Springs was a huge rail hub and offered plenty of opportunity. So far, the players have only battled a single werewolf, but they've had encounters (knowingly or unknowingly) with ghouls, ghosts, psychics, a fetch, a purified immortal, a brief foray into the Underworld, an exiled fae, vampires, and an unfettered geist. Not to mention other hunters, sherrifs, judges, and lawyers prosecuting them. The games only a handful of sessions in, but it really started to come into its own when the players decided to start recruiting people into Valkyrie, which made their operation seem more real as it it evolves from a tiny outpost into a field office. <br /> <br /> My players also stuck their safe house on top of Cheyenne Mountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2186-nerdynick","name":"Nerdynick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:25:05-07:00","id":913394,"title":"","content":"I also like Promethean. Trying to find out who you are while the territories do as well. That was the time for drifters.<br /> <br /> Also lots of great arguments for Demon.<br /> <br /> But like what about Mage? Discovery is a huge idea, instead of ancient mystery it can subtly change to a bit of exploration, also i do love weird West settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T19:03:01-07:00","id":913797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerdynick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/887498-the-american-west-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=913193#post913193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am currently running a Hunter game set in 1881 Colorado Springs. The characters are part of a fledgling Project Valkyrie that has sent cells out west as part of Operation Trailblazer, an attempt to discover how far and how deep the supernatural menace goes.<br /> <br /> Colorado Springs was a huge rail hub and offered plenty of opportunity. So far, the players have only battled a single werewolf, but they've had encounters (knowingly or unknowingly) with ghouls, ghosts, psychics, a fetch, a purified immortal, a brief foray into the Underworld, an exiled fae, vampires, and an unfettered geist. Not to mention other hunters, sherrifs, judges, and lawyers prosecuting them. The games only a handful of sessions in, but it really started to come into its own when the players decided to start recruiting people into Valkyrie, which made their operation seem more real as it it evolves from a tiny outpost into a field office.<br /> <br /> My players also stuck their safe house on top of Cheyenne Mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really awesome. I'd love to play in something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}